WEBVTT

00:00:28.733 --> 00:00:31.438
There are three types of irony out there.

00:00:31.438 --> 00:00:33.767
Situational irony is when you expect one thing,

00:00:33.767 --> 00:00:35.110
but get the opposite.

00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:37.804
Verbal irony is when someone says something,

00:00:37.804 --> 00:00:39.229
but truly means the opposite.

00:00:39.229 --> 00:00:40.858
Dramatic irony, though,

00:00:40.858 --> 00:00:42.824
is what we will be looking at right now.

00:00:42.824 --> 00:00:44.319
Dramatic irony is when the audience

00:00:44.319 --> 00:00:46.414
seems to know more about an event,

00:00:46.414 --> 00:00:47.529
a situation,

00:00:47.529 --> 00:00:48.864
or a conversation

00:00:48.864 --> 00:00:50.277
than the characters in the movie,

00:00:50.277 --> 00:00:51.240
on the show,

00:00:51.240 --> 00:00:52.708
or in the book do.

00:00:52.708 --> 00:00:54.620
The audience is in on a secret

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.455
that the characters have missed.

00:00:56.455 --> 00:00:57.936
This is a great story-telling device

00:00:57.936 --> 00:01:00.960
that creates tremendous emotion within that text.